~ start
President Larrañaga: His Majesty will receive you at four. Before that, ten minutes with me, so that we do not contradict each other in front of him.
- Ask about the Catalan question => catalan
- Ask about the new Spanish budget => budget
- Ask about Spain's role in the council => council
~ catalan
President Larrañaga: An internal matter, Mr President, and I say that with the tenderness one reserves for the subject.
- Offer discretion and silence => silence
- Say Europe will watch => watch
~ silence
President Larrañaga: Silence is the diplomacy of grown-ups. I will remember it when I am asked to do the same.
=> END
~ watch
President Larrañaga: Europe watches everything, and says nothing for as long as it is convenient. I would ask for convenience.
=> END
~ budget
President Larrañaga: We hold a fragile majority. A budget is a ten-month negotiation with nine friends who each want something different.
- Back their pension reform => pensions
- Back their defence line => defence_line
~ pensions
President Larrañaga: The pension reform is the hardest chapter. Your support will be quoted by both the left and the right, each wrongly.
=> END
~ defence_line
President Larrañaga: Defence, from Spain? A rare thing. My generals will be flattered and my partners will frown.
=> END
~ council
President Larrañaga: We hold three votes in the council and use them like a tapestry, slowly, and all at once.
- Ask them to back your file => back_file
- Offer to back theirs => their_file
~ back_file
President Larrañaga: Your file. I will weigh it with the wisdom of a man who has seen four presidents of France come and go.
=> END
~ their_file
President Larrañaga: You would back ours? Then I owe you a favour, and Spaniards pay their debts, usually in dinner.
=> END
